<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund bows to fan pressure and end Rheinmetall deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff88acbc16891a8a43b2262bf4762475a65575d50fd4917543d76845f1c03dbb</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121--2c9b64a964f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Borussia Dortmund has reluctantly ended its association with a major sponsor after long-term fan protests. They are not the first Bundesliga club to u-turn, as commercial interests clash with politics and fan culture.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich and Rwanda: A strategic climbdown?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e02a5f21d010f6cd48908409f3255be3b3616ec754712bab1d9704221fe9f25</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2025-08-14T17:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-and-rwanda-a-strategic-climbdown/a-73630410--dc539983a309.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-and-rwanda-a-strategic-climbdown/a-73630410?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At first glance, Bayern Munich's decision to end its commercial deal with Rwanda appears a rare moment of football morality. But dig a little deeper and the club's motivations seem not so straightforward.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The 50+1 rule in German football: What you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba8e1832ba2ac5083910c152d09cee3ce05726a65a806d31164802c40097ea11</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2025-06-18T10:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-50-1-rule-in-german-football-what-you-need-to-know/a-72952820--1c21d9ea7f6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-50-1-rule-in-german-football-what-you-need-to-know/a-72952820?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In Germany, the 50+1 rule protects professional football clubs from complete control by investors. This feature has many supporters internationally but also attracts criticism.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Grand Theft Auto VI launches to global fanfare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c358d4e32bf7e8c2adcc60a5801342de181b10814eacebbf3b0ed9956f3c0701</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T23:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/grand-theft-auto-vi-launches-to-global-fanfare/a-79986461--a4bcdbd4f395.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/grand-theft-auto-vi-launches-to-global-fanfare/a-79986461?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After 13 years of waiting, fans around the world will get to play the latest installment in the blockbuster video game series. In focus: A tale of crime and violence in a fictionalized version of Miami.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp and Wirtz offer glimpse of bright German future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e86490707719edbd882e4a418a739c8aeabc7d3f0b8a3d7c4d7a96b97c192412</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184--a5059b3200c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's fall from grace in recent years has seen the team drift away from the fans. But Monday's drubbing of the Netherlands and the impact of Jürgen Klopp, Florian Wirtz and emerging youngsters offers hope.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:364dfff25dea55708f3fa0830298743c96547237aabba3c89aa39c2f66c2416b</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229--458d3356c9f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp has joined the chorus of football figures critical of FIFA President Gianni Infantino. But with time running out, there are few who seem willing to run against him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey impasse as Russia threatens sanctions on Canada, Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed1523af7e6aae2b41a25fd13a0b1e571a77050c76395b930b67e027f6808ce2</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676--52aad908ad79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the CAS ordered ice hockey's governing body to reintegrate Russia into international play, a solution remains elusive. Now Russia has threatened to take legal action against two tournament hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Nmecha won't repeat controversial goal celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe01dd93f70ae9dce43fdb169888361b4012c167bfe19ea24ed7decde8202100</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994--cc5ab533247b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany head coach Jürgen Klopp has said midfielder Felix Nmecha will not repeat a goal celebration that sparked controversy over the past week. Germany are set to face Serbia and the Netherlands in the Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8539a046af592025f58dea02da59c24afb210201ec578751465f5f0e69de1225</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88f8269025894ca782f1efc82a72a937875f0cfba57f5559eaecfba60986e913</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Russia is back in world sport, but who is drug testing its athletes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:919eae9649440771979717b4469ca28c76958582b4812310c7ab2b65c5b5f98b</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467--6f0e1f90efa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has found that three-quarters of Russia's weightlifting team had no independent out-of-competition testing before this year's world championships, despite the country's doping history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e12041533f118678ca4d05050817fcf719e681990a0232ced084e5cc7c6a7199</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1237a22e8b81991e3b4407416c4a01bf87911c2bfdca6aac23d15fcb186dcb9</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
